    {
      "job_id": "93472091",
      "job_url": "https://ph.jobstreet.com/job/93472091?tracking=TMC-HirerMessageCandiMan-asia-6-jobtitle",
      "source": "JobStreet",
      "job_title": "Senior Full Stack Developer - 855391",
      "company": "Expansion International",
      "location": null,
      "application_status": "rejected",
      "fit_score": 45,
      "fit_summary": "Transferable full-stack fit through production .NET APIs, SQL Server business systems, React/Next.js, TypeScript, Docker, deployment, and operational support. The role's Java/Spring/WebFlux, GraphQL, GCP/GKE, and several modern frontend/testing requirements are not verified in the background.",
      "cover_letter_status": "drafted_with_gap_notice",
      "recruiter_name": "Dex Bayhon",
      "last_activity": "rejection_received",
      "next_action": "No further action; consider future roles with Expansion International if relevant.",
      "message_received_date": "2026-07-28",
      "response_sent_date": "2026-07-28",
      "notes": "Rejection email received from Dexter Bayhon, Recruitment Specialist at Expansion International, stating that the hiring manager selected another candidate whose background more closely aligned with the role's current needs.",
      "reply_draft": "Subject: Re: Senior Full Stack Developer - 855391\n\nHi Dex,\n\nThank you for reaching out and for the opportunity to provide more information about my background. Please see my answers below.\n\n1. Commercial software experience\nI have more than 15 years of experience building and supporting commercial and business-critical software, including production APIs, internal business systems, ERP workflows, customer portals, dashboards, and desktop applications. My responsibilities have covered requirements analysis, system and database design, backend and frontend development, API integration, deployment, troubleshooting, maintenance, and production support.\n\n2. Java, Spring, Spring Boot, and React\nMy primary professional backend experience is in C#, .NET, ASP.NET, and SQL Server. I also have some experience with Java and Spring, although I am not yet an expert in those technologies. My strong foundation in backend development, software architecture, React, and multiple programming environments allows me to become productive with new frameworks quickly. I have professional React experience with React and Next.js interfaces integrated with .NET REST APIs, authentication flows, dashboards, and data-driven workflows.\n\n3. Spring WebFlux\nMy production API experience has primarily been with .NET rather than Spring WebFlux. However, I have experience designing backend services, integrating APIs, supporting asynchronous application workflows, and maintaining production systems. These fundamentals are transferable to Spring WebFlux.\n\n4. GraphQL and REST APIs\nMy strongest API experience is with REST APIs using C# and .NET/ASP.NET. I have built and maintained APIs for business workflows, authentication, dashboards, integrations, and customer-facing applications, including deployment and production support. My direct GraphQL experience is limited, but my experience with API design, data modeling, authentication, and backend architecture gives me a strong foundation for adopting GraphQL.\n\n5. AI-assisted development\nI use ChatGPT and GitHub Copilot for code exploration, implementation, refactoring, test planning, documentation, and troubleshooting. I verify generated output through code review, requirements and architecture checks, builds and tests where available, and manual behavior validation. I remain responsible for the code’s correctness, security, and maintainability.\n\n6. GCP, GKE, Docker, and containerized applications\nI have hands-on experience with Docker, IIS, Windows Server, SQL Server, deployments, monitoring, server migrations, and production incident support. I have also used Google Cloud services for authentication in other projects, including configuring authentication flows and integrating them into applications. My GCP experience is focused on authentication rather than GKE administration or broader cloud infrastructure, while my strongest infrastructure experience is with Windows Server, IIS, Docker, and Azure DevOps workflows.\n\n7. Modern full-stack tools and frameworks\nMy professional experience includes TypeScript, React, Next.js, JavaScript, Vite, Tailwind CSS, Docker, Git, GitHub, Jira, xUnit, PostgreSQL, and production build and deployment workflows. My React projects use Vite, and I use GitHub extensively for source control, collaboration, and project delivery. My Flutter projects use Flutter’s Material design widgets.\n\nI have not used some of the other listed tools professionally, including React Material UI, Redux Toolkit, RTK Query, JOOQ, Redis, Flyway, Google Pub/Sub, GitHub Actions, Keycloak, Vitest, React Testing Library, Jest, Testcontainers, and Mockito. However, my experience across backend services, React development, testing, databases, and production delivery enables me to adopt new tools effectively.\n\n8. Earliest availability\nI am available to start immediately, subject to completing the hiring and onboarding process.\n\n9. CET-aligned schedule\nYes. I can commit to a full-time schedule aligned with Central European Time and the stated UK business hours, including the expected Philippine mid-shift schedule.\n\n10. Employment terms\nYes. I am amenable to the permanent, full-time, work-from-home arrangement, the PHP 140,000–150,000 gross monthly salary range, mandatory Philippine government contributions, and the stated benefits. I understand that I will need to use my own computer or laptop.\n\nMy strongest alignment is in production .NET backend and full-stack delivery, REST APIs, React/TypeScript, authentication integrations, Docker, deployment, and operational support. I would welcome the opportunity to contribute this experience while continuing to deepen my Java/Spring and Google Cloud expertise.\n\nThank you for your consideration. I look forward to hearing from you.\n\nBest regards,\nJustiniano Tagarda",
      "cover_letter": "Dear Hiring Team,\n\nI am applying for the Senior Full Stack Developer position. I am a senior full-stack developer with extensive experience building, maintaining, and supporting production business systems using C#, .NET, SQL Server, REST APIs, React, Next.js, and TypeScript.\n\nMy background aligns with the role's focus on delivering reliable full-stack applications and translating business requirements into practical software. I have built production APIs, SQL-backed workflows, dashboards, customer portals, and internal systems, while also handling frontend integration, deployments, troubleshooting, and ongoing production support. In my recent backend role, I improved .NET services and frontend data bindings, delivered a communications reporting dashboard, and led the migration of production websites, services, and SQL Server databases to new Windows Server infrastructure.\n\nWhile my recent professional experience is primarily in the .NET ecosystem rather than PHP/Symfony/Laravel, I bring a strong foundation in full-stack architecture, API integration, relational databases, business workflows, and operational ownership. I am comfortable learning an unfamiliar application stack and contributing where my existing experience can provide immediate value.\n\nI would welcome the opportunity to discuss how my production full-stack and business-systems experience could support your team. My resume is attached, and selected projects are available at https://justintagarda.com.\n\nThank you for your time and consideration.\n\nSincerely,\nJustiniano Tagarda"
    },
