    {
      "job_id": "93511011",
      "job_url": "https://ph.jobstreet.com/job/93511011?tracking=TMC-AbandonedApplyFlow-asia-6-jobtitle",
      "source": "JobStreet",
      "job_title": "Software Support Engineer | WFH | Mid Shift",
      "company": "Platserv PH / Platinum Outsourcing",
      "location": "Muntinlupa City, Metro Manila (Remote)",
      "application_status": "drafted",
      "fit_score": 60,
      "fit_summary": "Good transferable fit for software support, SQL-backed troubleshooting, production incident handling, Jira-based delivery, documentation, and remote client communication. Hands-on Python, Azure administration, Terraform/IaC, and Confluence experience were not verified.",
      "cover_letter_status": "drafted_with_gap_notice",
      "recruiter_name": null,
      "last_activity": "cover_letter_created",
      "next_action": "Review the Python, Azure, Terraform/IaC, and Confluence gaps before submitting.",
      "cover_letter": "Dear Hiring Team,\n\nI am applying for the Software Support Engineer position. I am a senior .NET backend and full-stack developer with extensive experience supporting production business systems, troubleshooting application and data issues, and translating operational needs into practical technical solutions.\n\nMy background aligns well with this role's focus on incident triage, diagnosis, resolution, documentation, and communication with clients and engineering teams. I have supported production APIs, SQL Server-backed workflows, dashboards, customer portals, and internal business applications. In my recent backend role, I monitored production infrastructure, provided incident support during service downtime, administered IIS and SQL Server environments, improved backend services and frontend data bindings, and led the migration of production websites, services, and databases to new Windows Server infrastructure.\n\nI also bring experience working directly with clients and stakeholders to clarify requirements, reproduce problems, define solutions, and deliver maintainable software. My verified tools and technologies include SQL, C#, .NET, REST APIs, React, TypeScript, Docker, IIS, Azure DevOps, Jira, and Git-based development workflows.\n\nMy recent experience is stronger in .NET and Microsoft-based production systems than in Python, Azure administration, and Terraform infrastructure-as-code. However, I have a solid foundation in application support, SQL troubleshooting, infrastructure operations, and learning new technical environments. I would welcome the opportunity to contribute that experience while growing into the role's broader support and cloud tooling requirements.\n\nMy résumé is attached, and selected projects are available at https://justintagarda.com. Thank you for your time and consideration.\n\nSincerely,\nJustiniano Tagarda"
    },
    {
      "job_id": "9ba0776704da86d2",
      "job_url": "https://ph.indeed.com/viewjob?jk=9ba0776704da86d2&from=shareddesktop_copy",
      "source": "Indeed",
      "job_title": "Freelance Developer - AI Product Prototyper & Knowledge System Specialist",
      "company": "OVATech OPC",
      "location": "Remote",
      "application_status": "applied",
      "fit_score": 50,
      "fit_summary": "Transferable fit through full-stack product development, frontend delivery, client requirements work, research-oriented problem solving, documentation, and AI-assisted development. No-code platforms, Notion knowledge management, Zapier/Make automation, and formal product-research experience were not verified.",
      "cover_letter_status": "drafted_with_gap_notice",
      "recruiter_name": null,
      "last_activity": "application_submitted",
      "next_action": "Wait for employer response.",
      "cover_letter": "Dear Hiring Team,\n\nI am applying for the Freelance Developer position focused on AI product prototyping and knowledge systems. I am a senior full-stack developer with extensive experience turning business ideas and requirements into usable web applications, dashboards, workflows, and production software using C#, .NET, React, Next.js, TypeScript, and REST APIs.\n\nMy background aligns with the role's need for someone who can work independently, organize complex information, learn new tools quickly, and turn concepts into structured, actionable product work. I have worked directly with clients to define scope, clarify requirements, refine functionality, and deliver maintainable software. I have also built data-driven interfaces, authentication flows, dashboards, internal business systems, and customer portals, while supporting projects through deployment, troubleshooting, and ongoing improvement.\n\nI am comfortable researching unfamiliar domains, synthesizing requirements, documenting workflows, and collaborating closely with stakeholders. I also regularly use AI-assisted development tools and have a strong interest in applying emerging technologies to improve product delivery and business processes.\n\nMy verified experience is strongest in custom web application development rather than specific no-code platforms such as Notion, Webflow, Zapier, or Make. However, my product-development background gives me a solid technical foundation for learning those tools, organizing knowledge systems, building prototypes, and evaluating practical automation opportunities.\n\nI would welcome the opportunity to support your product initiatives and work closely with the founder to turn ideas into clear, useful, and continuously improving solutions. My résumé is attached, and selected projects are available at https://justintagarda.com.\n\nThank you for your time and consideration.\n\nSincerely,\nJustiniano Tagarda"
